{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1aa62b3f9bf573abec8aaa02356bec1f8463366f73aac39a829e198d15b6c490","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_29e3e7c890c770a08e43781e7137e67c99bb57f9f8a5bb61c836cd547658ee3b","slc_9bc3c87d28ec027230d1c92dc4be555f9500c37ecc6f79879b21a3cb227851b8"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Atomic implements the Agent Skills standard and can use configured Claude Code or Codex skill directories without rewriting them; skills can be auto-selected from descriptions or invoked with /skill:<name>.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3b8355bc5017ac70fa08cf5c29fe3b69fc3c4030b40832ab0d959edf0f488e8e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d53dcf3fe808886d56440d04fe49d4addbb866933e4ececb6f58b5e1ebadcad6","slc_d5f54b047556737cc891c5fa8b173bc1b906d03965df1d87dfd71ec0fa1b75e7","slc_eafe1aa3fc6ab424482cec8c847ae5a37bf6f70849c42d4921176eb7d1f50d18"],"source_ids":["src_33a6f061b716592a96f00a65a03e696a"],"text":"The terminal UI uses a Catppuccin Mocha role-mapped palette with Catppuccin Blue as the sole accent, status colors mapped one-to-one to orchestrator session statuses, and Unicode-only iconography with no emoji.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3ed2955cbcbfe13de480288197471e8a07f4f1b57883a3b3367d18588f7f5676","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_66d7e12d9135bab082423414f6e19370a76e3766eb8bb9d5cd31effa4feb00e4","slc_941db28ccbe7718c43dfd57dfa7a43a56256f2cd50e3f2ee1f0141c164a61f9c"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Atomic is a fork of Pi and works with providers, tools, MCP servers, skills, and extensions from an existing Pi stack; it connects to model providers directly rather than wrapping other coding tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_414978fb23471071bb022d4cf608c86ee6867ee13e6ad9a60d81d0ca52c71f69","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a3f2cc43d6f59efe8419f76d22aece04864ff5f2aff2b623a372fea666bc272"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Workflows persist artifacts such as plans, logs, transcripts, reviewer notes, check output, and summaries; research commonly lives in research/ and specs in specs/.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4ae536c8d4bfc6d3685b31f4c3e160a2720366ec7111e1f4906e8089e5fe2a13","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3c8b89b227deebcfe996953603a92f481ff5d17e3b12311bbafa988ef62831ec","slc_68347bc0d2800f8a336f5e49ebafaacffb7f0113f124d8027e00fbed993ebfe1"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"The Linux musl release archives bundle their C++ runtime and run on stock Alpine, but Android and Termux are unsupported; provider availability depends on credentials, subscription, region, and the provider catalog.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4f8d76953140fdfd7d146670d8c5e9dd2a9c28a6595be59bc45bb0036bcc6a23","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_156ec63351ba3b6e75ea3af9aef71d0e93add87a9f1ff04ef358e2e619e837d5","slc_59ba90feba969f66f8cd6e893a3754e14f5b0bb62bbcdc92626d7c2ba8e16104"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Stages can prompt an agent, run tools, call MCP servers, save artifacts, branch, retry, run in parallel, or pause for approval; specialized subagents handle focused work while a parent agent or workflow controls the larger task.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_55718a22ece9d6a122c394ad39ed3fdc21cdd4afca19a238bc2dde8da0525145","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b0065672901d84e1513cccb85020d4e8d8735f46e4575d16fa25ea1d13eea45c"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"The CLI exposes workflow management commands including /workflow list, inputs, status, connect, quit, and resume; quitting pauses a run so it can resume later.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_754d00b01ed591828812e41971dfb6f30ace674d7ad6e0e7691abc9118ef4d82","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_05be5b0bc1f83ad5249fb09ec9f6f2866996c367b400e5f219e3d71bce31df1c","slc_ca1f322c8bf87101f435f7de3c993cf9b0e5057a0e119c0fa3ae3dd46911f2d4","slc_ed746526c6c7d5de0c278365190e132c8e9839407cede569dc5c12f79c5f68f4"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Atomic ships three top-level building blocks: workflows, skills, and specialized subagents, with nine bundled subagent definitions such as worker, debugger, and codebase-analyzer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7f35ecc6278348c7f94936dc04ee74c2e91852fbd716819ceb6918d9e18075db","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_48233a33b7569b20c640070a33ce2037d89139dbb2e76fd189193e1545f2bdde"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Non-interactive use is supported via atomic -p \"<prompt>\", which prints the response and exits; provider credentials are stored in ~/.atomic/agent/auth.json with owner-only permissions where the platform supports them.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8b6d78c7883d39f4daaed1ea64c035cbcc03b56b98af96984f64eee318396bd2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8fbb245ff172ba426627ac76b1db3c1c8f4ebfd60b8bd595e6052a8c73e1762f","slc_b494d451c61ed44add8917ff27035e52dc81de1eed557527a646d540724288a2"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Package installation requires Node.js 22.19 or newer plus npm, pnpm, Yarn, or Bun (Bun 1.4.2+ for Bun installs); a self-contained release archive path needs no Node.js or package manager.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c6de7e1d48e5a0b82ad01433fe0a14b228ae2cee14bd2f607cafe5a17e4e34cb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_224c1c98f3c8735f203c4e274714da33da546fe6be9a6ee7020ebe489a777906","slc_dc97fd28278a34f9a57cf8e7d67051080012e2710706336ede13d0ec157f074a"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Workflows are authored as TypeScript workflow({...}) definitions whose stage dependencies must form a directed acyclic graph; cyclic graphs are unsupported, and loop/repair iterations must create distinct tracked work per iteration.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e4867eaf18a8eb7ef33839806768004447c1628fc545d196f5445953c2c808d4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"bastani-inc/atomic@ca64fa07885f snapshot cc096d4fbf9ff28b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6e1c51f3f724898304a9db21af1fac3cc336face09b362df99c520214f2466cb"],"source_ids":["src_a79e9df099a05d4196058e640a174b9b"],"text":"Atomic has no built-in sandbox or command-level shell permission gate; tools and extensions run with the user's permissions, and the README recommends running autonomous work in a devcontainer, VM, or remote machine.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:05:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_727ce1c0c25c4a01934302190a6fcebc"}
